    {
      "post_id": 33791,
      "author_username": "calen",
      "author_user_id": 155,
      "timestamp_iso": "2017-06-06T04:01:42+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1496721702000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Jun 5, 2017 23:01:42 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Bringing another thread back from the archives! I remember seeing this post back in the day and being really blown away by Mike's clone - so much so that I remade the exact cross in 2014. I didn't keep nearly enough of the seedlings (many of you out there probably have even better clones than the one below!), but this plant stood out for its extra dark color and bronzy lid similar to Mike's clone. It's still immature (no flowers yet) and will continue to darken - very excited to see any July-August traps it puts out! S. flava var. ornata (Gulf Coast x Black Veins Bulloch Co. GA Clone B):<br/><a href=\"http://s1329.photobucket.com/user/calenhall/media/IMG_5771_zpsxzbfnbzw.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1329.photobucket.com/albums/w549/calenhall/IMG_5771_zpsxzbfnbzw.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/><a href=\"http://s1329.photobucket.com/user/calenhall/media/IMG_5773_zpsye5ax7zi.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1329.photobucket.com/albums/w549/calenhall/IMG_5773_zpsye5ax7zi.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/>",
      "body_text": "Bringing another thread back from the archives! I remember seeing this post back in the day and being really blown away by Mike's clone - so much so that I remade the exact cross in 2014. I didn't keep nearly enough of the seedlings (many of you out there probably have even better clones than the one below!), but this plant stood out for its extra dark color and bronzy lid similar to Mike's clone. It's still immature (no flowers yet) and will continue to darken - very excited to see any July-August traps it puts out! S. flava var. ornata (Gulf Coast x Black Veins Bulloch Co. GA Clone B):",
